meta {
  name: Login (OIDC)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/auth/login?org=provincie-voorbeeld&redirect=/
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  org: provincie-voorbeeld
  redirect: /
}

docs {
  Initiates the OIDC authorization code flow (with PKCE, S256) for the
  named organisation. Only active in production when APP_DEV_MODE=false
  and the org has been configured via POST /api/v1/orgs/:slug/oidc.

  Query params:
    org       required — organisation slug (must match an org row with
              OIDC configured)
    redirect  optional — URL to return to after successful login;
              defaults to /

  Flow:
    1. Look up the org and resolve its OIDC issuer/client config.
    2. Generate a PKCE code_verifier + state nonce.
    3. Store both in a short-lived (5 min) signed state cookie
       (saidkick_state).
    4. 302 redirect to the IdP's authorization_endpoint with
       response_type=code, scope=openid email profile, PKCE challenge.

  Responses:
    302 Found     — redirect to the IdP login page
    400           — org query param missing
    404           — organisation not found
    400           — OIDC not configured for this org
    502           — could not reach the OIDC provider discovery endpoint

  NOTE: This endpoint is a browser redirect — it cannot be exercised
  meaningfully inside Bruno's request runner. Use a browser or curl -L.
}
